# What Vercel must NOT upload, for either of the two projects built from this repo
# (trackr-backend and trackr-frontend, each with its own Root Directory -- see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md steps 2 and 4).
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE. Vercel deploys from git, so an UNTRACKED file is
# already never deployed -- demo.html, landing.html, analytics-demo.html and the
# root-level BLUEPRINT/TARGET_FLOW/OPEN_QUESTIONS notes are all untracked today and were
# never in a deployment. They are listed anyway so that committing one later does not
# silently start shipping it.
#
# WHETHER THIS FILE DOES ANYTHING depends on one Vercel project setting: "Include source
# files outside of the Root Directory in the Build Step". With it OFF, only
# trackr-backend/ (or trackr-frontend/) is uploaded and everything below is already
# excluded by construction -- this file is then a harmless no-op. With it ON, which is
# the monorepo default, the whole repo is uploaded and this file is what prunes it.
# There are no .md files and no tests INSIDE either project directory (checked), so
# per-project .vercelignore files would be empty; this one at the repo root is the only
# one that can do any work.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, because something reads it:
#   fixtures/   96K, and app/db/seed_demo.py resolves fixtures/demo_portfolio.json from
#               the repo root at runtime, so `python -m app.db.seed_demo` against a
#               deployed database keeps working. The rest of the directory is test data
#               and could be pruned, but 96K does not justify a per-file negation rule.
#               Note app/db/load_golden.py's fixtures/golden_portfolio.json is gitignored
#               and has therefore never been in a deployment at all.
#   schema/, contracts/   no code reads them (every reference in app/ is a docstring),
#               but CLAUDE.md treats them as the language-agnostic definition of the
#               system, and they cost almost nothing to carry.

# ---- documentation: never executed, never served ----------------------------------
*.md
docs/

# ---- the test suite: nothing in a deployment imports it ---------------------------
tests/

# ---- planning and prompt material, not part of the product ------------------------
plan/
prompts/

# ---- standalone mockup pages, superseded by the real frontend ---------------------
demo.html
analytics-demo.html
landing.html

# ---- local-only tooling and scratch space -----------------------------------------
local/
Makefile
start.sh
stop.sh
